astling improves king safety and connects rooks; highly desirable given White's developing initiative.\n- N: b8-c6 – Develops the knight to a natural square, supports d4/e5 breaks and prepares for central play.\n\nAmong these, **K: e8-g8** stands out because king safety is paramount, especially with White’s knight already on g5. Not castling soon risks tactical blows like Ng5xf7 or discovered attacks. Additionally, castling is time-sensitive—once the center opens, it may become unsafe.\n\nReason: Castling now ensures king safety, activates the h8 rook via R: h8-f8 or -g8 later, and is consistent with opening principles. Delaying it risks losing the right due to check or positional constraints.\n\nAnswer: K: e8-g8"}
