) or it's a forced stalemate. However, **with only kings left, checkmate is impossible**.\n\nTherefore, the game is theoretically drawn. But to maximize winning chances (e.g., if opponent blunders), we aim to **stalemate the opponent or force them into a corner**.\n\nBest practical approach: Use active king placement to provoke errors.\n\nReason: K: e3-f3 places the black king one square in front of White’s king (on f1), preparing to take the opposition if White moves to f2. This maximizes restriction and mimics winning endgame technique.\n\nAnswer: K: e3-f3"}
